WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.267
-You're not on social medias.

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.501
-I'm not on social media,
no, I'm not.

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.334
-At all. That's a choice
or you just...?

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:06.534
-I just don't -- I can't --

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:07.934
I don't have the energy for it,
I think.

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:10.601
-Yeah. Never got into it?
-No, but I like the stuff --

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:13.033
Some of my friends will send me
stuff that makes me laugh,

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:14.667
and that's...
-Like a text or an e-mail.

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:16.067
-Yeah, something.

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:17.934
-So you can't really
get away from it all.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:20.367
-I can't really
get away from it all, no.

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:22.033
But they'll send
some funny things.

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.767
Because they're all degenerates,
my friends.

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:25.267
-Yeah, exactly. I'm friends
with some of your friends.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:27.000
-Yeah.
-I found something that I would

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.634
send to you
if you were on social media.

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:30.133
-Okay, show me.

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:31.934
-This is from "New York"
magazine, a great magazine.

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:33.167
It's "The Cut." It says...

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:36.367
"Sam Rockwell is...
Totally Kind of Hot?"

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:37.901
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, I like the...

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:39.400
-You like this?

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.367
-...the enthusiasm and then
the trepidation kind of.

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:43.868
-No, this is all --
-"Totally kind of."

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:46.968
-No, this is a full-on --
This is a great article for you.

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:49.400
"Sam Rockwell is
Totally Kind of Hot?"

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.300
-I'll take it.
I'll take "kind of."

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.934
-You want no question mark?
-No, I'll take it. Listen.

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:56.067
-You want an exclamation point.

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:58.868
-I'll take whatever I can get.
You know what I mean?

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:01.000
-I could see
the trepidation there, yeah.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.200
It would bum me out.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.467
-No, but "totally" is great.

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:05.567
And then "kind of" --
You know.

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:07.501
-But -- And the question mark
is a bummer, too.

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:09.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:12.868
I was on a golf magazine once,

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:15.033
and it says,
"Jimmy Fallon Plays Golf?"

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.601
-And then
there's a question mark?

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:17.834
-A question mark.
-Golf?

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:19.534
You're like,
"Why wouldn't I play golf, man?"

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:20.934
-I'm on the cover
of this magazine!

00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:23.133
You better play golf.
What am I there for?

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:24.267
-Listen.
It could be worse, you know?

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:27.367
-Yeah, I guess.
"Kind of Plays Golf?"

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:29.701
[ Laughter ]
Could it be worse?

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:31.901
Can we talk about
"The Bad Guys"?

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:33.133
-Yes, "Bad Guys."

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:34.601
-This is gonna be a giant movie
this week.

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:36.467
-Coming out soon.
This is a really fun movie.

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:41.300
And we spent a long time
doing it, and it's fun.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.400
-The premise is great.
-It's really fun.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.601
It's an Australian comic book.
-Yeah.

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:48.968
Where all the bad guys
get together and they go,

00:01:48.968 --> 00:01:50.434
"Hey, what if we were good?"

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:53.300
-Yeah, they try to turn good.
-"What if we can be good?

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.968
And they --
It feels good to do good.

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:56.801
-Yeah.
-And let's see if we can do it."

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:58.934
And, well, we'll see
if they can do it or not.

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:00.767
-Yeah.
It's kind of like they're --

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:03.534
It's kind of like an
"Ocean's 11" for kids, I guess.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:05.300
Or, like,
a "Reservoir Dogs" for kids.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.334
-It is like a "Reservoir Dogs"
for kids, yeah.

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:10.100
It's really good.
You know, I love your dancing.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.901
I always make you dance
every time you come on

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:13.701
even if you don't want to.

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:15.767
So I appreciate you doing it
and humoring me.

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:18.734
But in this movie,
your character, Mr. Wolf,

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:20.267
is actually a great dancer.

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:22.534
And you actually
got the director

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:23.801
to hire a choreographer?

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:25.267
-Yeah.
-For the cartoon?

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:27.133
-Well, they wanted to really
make it real, so they --

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:29.167
Unfortunately, Zazie and I
couldn't get together.

00:02:29.167 --> 00:02:30.834
She was not -- just on a --

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:32.501
We were in different parts
of the world.

00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:34.734
But they got Susie Misner, who
choreographed "Fosse/Verdon."

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.767
So she put it --
Susie put it together.

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:39.968
And she knows some of my moves,
and she --

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:42.767
We wanted to get together
with Zazie and Susie,

00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:44.934
but we never had the time
and stuff, so...

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:47.300
-It's fantastic.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.100
Here's a peek at "The Bad Guys."
Take a look at this.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.567
♪♪

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:55.133
-They stole the Golden Dolphin!

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.868
-Come on. You can't prove that.

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:59.100
[ Clang ]

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:01.234
-My baby!

00:03:01.234 --> 00:03:04.133
-On your knees, bad guys,
with your hands up!

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:06.267
-Never! We're outta here!

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:08.801
♪♪

00:03:08.801 --> 00:03:11.067
-So long, suckas!

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:13.400
♪♪

00:03:17.367 --> 00:03:19.667
-Well, this just got
a little weird.

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:21.367
-that's exactly right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.767
-Yeah, hey.
-Sam Rockwell, everybody!

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:26.601
"The Bad Guys"
hits theaters Friday!

00:03:26.601 --> 00:03:29.033
And check out "American Buffalo"
when you can,

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:31.801
over at the
Circle in the Square Theatre.

